# Project-level exclusions for the review gate.
# Copy to `.claude/hooks/review-exclude.txt`. One grep -E regex per line.
# Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# The hook already excludes the obvious non-code: docs, *.md, lock files, CI
# config, and (unless you opt in) tests/. What it cannot know is which paths in
# YOUR repo are generated, vendored, or data.

# Generated artifacts — reviewing them reviews the generator's output, not code
^dist/
^build/
^target/

# Vendored third-party code — not yours to review
/vendor/
/node_modules/

# Append-only data files — every commit touches them, none of it is logic
\.jsonl$

# ⚠️ Do NOT exclude things merely because they are noisy in review.
# Two categories look excludable but are not:
#   - Test fixtures that assertions read from. If a fixture list goes wrong,
#     the mutation test goes green while testing nothing.
#   - Config that changes runtime behaviour (feature flags, thresholds).
#     "It's just config" is how a threshold change ships unreviewed.
